 "stop": "3 quatrains",
 "poem": "This Thursday, you left away\nYour soul to wake from sleepless day,\nThe rest of us, all for ours we.\nThus while the dust and splendour's glory\nBefore our eyes flashed o'er creation,\nEach soul grew lonely, afraid\nTo leave behind it even in creation,\nHeaving and struggling with dismay.\nYet know I that when the dawn is again\nThe sun shall rise up on all things awake,\nAnd waking wings shall from deeps unfold creation,\nRaising the soft shadowy sun",
